  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Express $111111$ as the product of four two-digit numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$111111=21\\times11\\times13\\times37$.\n\nGroup the prime factors $3$ and $7$ to make the fourth two-digit factor.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}111111&=3\\times37037\\\\111111&=3\\times7\\times5291\\\\111111&=3\\times7\\times11\\times481\\\\111111&=3\\times7\\times11\\times13\\times37.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe factors $11$, $13$ and $37$ are already two-digit numbers. Combine $3$ and $7$ to obtain $21$.\n\n$$111111=21\\times11\\times13\\times37.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
